<article class="env-lemma" id="0H6N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H6N">Lemma <span data-tag="0H6N">62.14.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[r]_ f \ar[d] &  X \ar[d] \\  Y' \ar[r]^ g &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a cartesian diagram of schemes locally of finite type over $S$ with $g$ proper. Let $r, e \geq 0$. Let $\alpha $ be a family of $r$-cycles on the fibres of $X/Y$. Let $\beta '$ be a family of $e$-cycles on the fibres of $Y'/S$. Then we have $f_*(g^*(\alpha ) \circ \beta ') = \alpha \circ g_*\beta '$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Unwinding the definitions, this follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0H6B" data-tag="0H6B">62.12.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>